# Military education (P5.5) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup and host start: see payments.http / users.http.
# Prerequisites: an active term with a military_education subject + group (scheduling.http or lifecycle.http),
# a student with the student role, and the admin login below.
#
# Flow: apply/assign → pending_payment registration → military fee appears → office/online payment
#       → PaymentCompleted → registration becomes registered and the student appears in the roster.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminEmail = admin@cu.edu.eg
@adminPassword = paste-SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD-here

@facultyId = paste-faculty-id
@termId = paste-term-id
@militaryGroupId = paste-military-subject-group-id
@studentId = paste-student-id
@studentToken = paste-student-access-token

### 1. Log in as the seeded admin → copy "accessToken" into @token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2. Define the term's military-education fee (once; also needed by apply)
# @name militaryFee
POST {{host}}/api/admin/fee-items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Military education",
  "nameAr": "التربية العسكرية",
  "description": "Military-education registration fee",
  "category": "military_education",
  "amount": 500,
  "termId": "{{termId}}",
  "facultyId": null,
  "departmentId": null,
  "dueOn": "2099-12-31"
}

###
@feeItemId = {{militaryFee.response.body.$.id}}

### 3. Optional: switch the faculty to mandatory mode (then students cannot apply; use assign below)
PUT {{host}}/api/admin/faculties/{{facultyId}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "militaryEducationPolicy": { "mode": "mandatory" } }

### 4. Student applies (opt-in mode only) → 201 pending_payment
# @name apply
POST {{host}}/api/military-education/apply
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectGroupId": "{{militaryGroupId}}" }

### 5. The student sees the fee to pay
GET {{host}}/api/payments/fees?termId={{termId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 6. Student Affairs assigns students (works in any mode) → per-student outcomes
POST {{host}}/api/admin/military-education/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentIds": ["{{studentId}}"],
  "subjectGroupId": "{{militaryGroupId}}"
}

### 7. Resync pending fee requests of the term (safe to repeat; `republished` is the pending count)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/military-education/resync?termId={{termId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Record the office payment in full → registration confirmed
POST {{host}}/api/admin/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "{{studentId}}",
  "feeItemId": "{{feeItemId}}",
  "amount": 500,
  "method": "cash",
  "reference": "MIL-2026-0001",
  "paidAt": null
}

### 9. The registration is now registered and the student is in the roster
GET {{host}}/api/registration/mine?termId={{termId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/admin/groups/{{militaryGroupId}}/roster
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
